# M06: Additive maintenance and computing/network status panels. Graph planning only.
# M05: Additive ECLSS diagnostic allocation, not pressure-rated or service-access verified.
# M04: Added conceptual fixed-hull telemetry cabinets; historical M03 geometry preserved.
# No qualified hardware dimensions; discrete thermal loop modelling is in external model files.
# M03: Original telescope, truss, habitat and structural rules remain unchanged.
# The sensor/valve housings are illustrative external diagnostics, NOT pressure penetrations.
# MERIDIAN SYSTEMS CUTAWAY / M02 AIRLOCK REFIT
# Additive planning arrangement based on Meridian_Service_Refit.p3d.
# Source telescopes, repaired trusses, exterior circular hatch, and three fins retained.
# The original airlock barrel is deliberately refit with a real side aperture.
# A keeps its original full bore and closed cap; B is a crew-sized bypass.
# Start arguments: habitat period, exterior hatch angle, B hatch angle (degrees).
# Default all doors are closed; A operations are schematic until stow qualification.
# The 14 MWh battery allocation does not establish cabinet density or certification.
# Hull placeholders use open sectional skins; return tubes have annular open ends.
# Rooms/equipment, utility routes, and fusion components are proposed concepts.
# No pressure, radiation, reactor, collision, food-closure or thermal certification.
# The source rotation period remains 60 s. Change Start to select another period.
# Native materials and geometry; no external meshes or reference image atlas.
# MERIDIAN  /  Port-bow reference reconstruction
# Volumetric native ProGen3D grammar. The optical barrels, truss corners, habitat and radiators
# retain the original port-bow composition. The pressure body now uses physical circular sections.
# Native camera point (0 0 0), direction (0 0 -1), up (0 1 0), centred principal point.
# Horizontal focal ratio 930/1100; 36 mm sensor, 30.43636 mm lens; frame 1672 x 941.
# The active Start includes the planet and rings. Use MeridianShip(60) alone to inspect the ship.
# Design span is approximately 900 m. Both scene branches share the same scale.
# Observatory argument is the habitat rotation period in seconds. Default pose at t=0.
# Foil seams, extra truss webbing and rim panels are thin 3-D extrusions fitted to the observed contours.
# 3-D solids and surface panels only. The grammar has no external mesh dependencies.
# Service refit. Start parameters are habitat period (seconds) and exterior hatch swing (degrees).
# Use hatch angle 0 for closed or 105 for fully open. The inner hatch is modelled closed.
Start -> MeridianAirlockRefit(60 0 0)

MeridianServiceScene(period hatchAngle) ->
    [ MeridianConfiguredShip(period hatchAngle) ]
    [ S(0.8018569936 0.8018569936 0.8018569936) RingedGiant ]

PortBowScene(period) -> [ MeridianShip(period) ] [ S(0.8018569936 0.8018569936 0.8018569936) RingedGiant ]
MeridianShip(period) -> MeridianConfiguredShip(period 105)
MeridianConfiguredShip(period hatchAngle) -> [ S(0.8018569936 0.8018569936 0.8018569936) Observatory(period hatchAngle 0) ]

ThermalBlanket ->
    BlanketFaces(12)
    FoilClamps(12)

